  "source": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>FAQ Section</title>\n  <script type=\"application/json\" id=\"effect-meta\">\n  {\n    \"id\": \"combo-faq-accordion-section\",\n    \"title\": \"FAQ Section\",\n    \"summary\": \"A heading with native disclosure questions.\",\n    \"description\": \"A heading with native disclosure questions.\",\n    \"theme\": \"combos-recipes\",\n    \"categories\": [\"combo\", \"section\"],\n    \"tags\": [\"combo\", \"block\", \"faq\", \"accordion\", \"details\", \"section\"],\n    \"tech\": [\"css\"],\n    \"era\": \"2020s\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"intermediate\",\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"browser_support\": \"All modern browsers (Chromium, Firefox, Safari).\",\n    \"performance_notes\": \"Lightweight — composited transform/opacity work only.\",\n    \"accessibility_notes\": \"Composed blocks keep real landmarks and heading levels so the section still makes sense in a document outline.\",\n    \"customization\": [\n      { \"name\": \"--bg\", \"description\": \"Panel background\", \"default\": \"#151b2a\" }\n    ],\n    \"variations\": [\"Reskin through the custom properties\", \"Swap the copy for your own\"],\n    \"ai_usage\": \"FAQ and support pages. Native details gives keyboard support, in-page search, and correct disclosure semantics — an ARIA accordion has to reimplement all three.\"\n  }\n  </script>\n  <style>\n    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; }\n    body { background: #0b0d12; color: #e7ebf3;\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif; }\n    body { display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 2rem 1rem; }\n    .wrap { width: min(92vw, 310px); }\n    .wrap h2 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.4rem; }\n    details { border-radius: 12px; background: #151b2a; border: 1px solid #263149; margin-bottom: 8px; overflow: hidden; }\n    summary { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; padding: .8rem 1rem;\n      cursor: pointer; font-size: .9rem; list-style: none; }\n    summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }\n    summary .ch { color: #8b93a7; transition: transform .25s; }\n    details[open] summary .ch { transform: rotate(45deg); }\n    details p { margin: 0; padding: 0 1rem 1rem; color: #8b93a7; font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.6; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <section class=\"wrap\"><h2>Frequently asked</h2>\n  <details open><summary>Can I use these commercially? <span class=\"ch\">＋</span></summary><p>Yes — everything is MIT licensed, including the generated metadata.</p></details>\n  <details><summary>Do effects need a build step? <span class=\"ch\">＋</span></summary><p>No. Each specimen is one HTML file that runs from the filesystem.</p></details>\n  <details><summary>How do agents consume it? <span class=\"ch\">＋</span></summary><p>Through the JSON API or the bundled MCP server.</p></details></section>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
